course: dictionary
lesson: 3612
title: Fill: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «The room filled with people» means the room became full. «Fill in the form» means write what is missing.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. In «A howler monkey booms so loud it fills the building», fills means the sound makes the building full. It does not mean the monkey is filling a jug with water.
explain: Fill also has a maths use. If a baker fills 6 trays with 8 buns each, you can work out the total with 6 × 8, which is 48 buns. Look for clues like «each» or «in all» to know it is a sum.
fact: Fill means to put in as much as something can hold.
fact: Fill up means to make something completely full.
fact: To fill in a form or a gap is to write what is missing.
fact: «Filled with» tells you what is inside, as in «The jar was filled with sweets».
fact: In a maths problem, «fills N jars with K each» means you multiply N × K to find the total.
exercise: «Stories grow because people fill gaps with guesses.» What does fill gaps mean here? | Sell the gaps | Walk through the gaps | Make the gaps bigger | *Put guesses into the missing parts of the story
exercise: A baker fills 6 trays with 8 buns each. How many buns are there in all? | 68 | *48 | 2 | 14
exercise: Which phrase means write the missing words? | *Fill in the blanks | Fill up the jug | Fill the bath
test: «Waterholes fill with animals in the cool of morning and evening.» What does fill with mean here? | *Become crowded with | Pour water into | Sleep beside | Forget about
test: «A submarine fills its tanks with water to sink.» What does fills its tanks mean? | Paints them | Cleans the windows | *Puts as much water in as they can hold | Empties them out
exam: In «Charles Darwin filled notebooks on his round-the-world voyage», what does filled mean? | *Wrote in them until every page was full | Lost them at sea | Bought them in a shop | Read them quickly
